---
import DotAgentsHighlight from '@components/DotAgentsHighlight.astro';
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="With Agents — Practical coding-agent workflows"
  description="A source-backed field guide to coding-agent workflows: recognizing AI slop, writing capable co-worker briefs, preserving durable context, demanding proof, right-sizing threads, coordinating agent work, and measuring outcomes."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-24">
    <section class="space-y-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-indigo-600">
        Practical coding-agent workflows
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-light leading-tight text-gray-950">
          A practical field guide for agentic coding in 2026.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-gray-600 font-light leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
          With Agents is a source-backed series about coding agents: how to recognize AI slop, brief capable but context-limited agents, preserve repo-local knowledge, demand risk-scaled evidence, coordinate agent work, and measure outcomes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
        <a href="/posts/what-is-ai-slop" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-gray-900 px-5 py-3 text-white transition-colors duration-200 hover:bg-gray-700 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
          Start with AI slop
        </a>
        <a href="/resources/coding-with-agents" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-5 py-3 text-gray-800 transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-gray-400 hover:bg-gray-50 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
          Browse resources
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-6">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-indigo-600">
          Core entry points
        </p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-light text-gray-900">
          Start by the problem you need to solve.
        </h2>
        <p class="max-w-3xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          These primary entry points cover AI slop, assignment design, the current landscape, durable context, risk-scaled proof, and useful handoffs. The full posts index also covers interface design, tool case studies, agent coordination, and outcome measurement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <a href="/posts/what-is-ai-slop" class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 transition-all duration-200 hover:border-gray-300 hover:shadow-lg focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-600">AI quality</p>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-light text-gray-900">What Is AI Slop?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A plain-language test for generated output that only looks finished: unclear purpose, little evidence, missing ownership, and hidden work.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/posts/capable-coworker-coding-agents" class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 transition-all duration-200 hover:border-gray-300 hover:shadow-lg focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-600">Assignment brief</p>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-light text-gray-900">Brief the Agent Like a Capable Co-Worker</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A practical model for assigning work, supplying missing context, defining verification, and keeping authority and accountability with people.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/posts/agentic-coding-2026" class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 transition-all duration-200 hover:border-gray-300 hover:shadow-lg focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-600">Series map</p>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-light text-gray-900">Agentic Coding in 2026</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A practical field guide to cheap implementation, alignment, proof, useful friction, codebase infrastructure, context hygiene, and factory-era workflows.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/posts/durable-context-coding-agents" class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 transition-all duration-200 hover:border-gray-300 hover:shadow-lg focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-600">Context anchor</p>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-light text-gray-900">Your Repo Is the Memory</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A field guide for keeping coding agents aligned with repo-local truth, shared state, proof, and human judgment.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/posts/make-the-agent-prove-it" class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 transition-all duration-200 hover:border-gray-300 hover:shadow-lg focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-600">Proof contract</p>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-light text-gray-900">Make the Agent Prove It</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A risk-scaled acceptance contract for discriminating tests, real-system checks, external oracles, evidence packets, boundaries, and review.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/posts/right-sized-threads-durable-state" class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 transition-all duration-200 hover:border-gray-300 hover:shadow-lg focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-600">Workflow practice</p>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-light text-gray-900">Right-Sized Threads, Durable State</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">How to keep connected work together, start fresh at clear responsibility boundaries, and synchronize threads through repository state.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <DotAgentsHighlight />
  </div>
</Layout>
